                                "sense_id": "b5569be9-67a2-35de-8a03-5fd08d66e50d",
                                "text": "When Zoylus was sicke, he knew not where / Saue his wrought night cap, and laune Pillow-bere:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14d79d80-911e-4010-b1e7-5f20bfb4fc75",
                                "sense_id": "b5569be9-67a2-35de-8a03-5fd08d66e50d",
                                "text": "Ne was there such another Pardoner, For in his male had he a pillowbere, Which as he sayd was our Ladyes vayle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9748bb3-e5a0-4a36-a1a6-84ab64066bbf",
                                "sense_id": "b5569be9-67a2-35de-8a03-5fd08d66e50d",
                                "text": "she had so well covered herself with a pillowbeer which she there found, that her regard to decency was not in the least violated by the presence of so many men as were now in the room."
                            }
